From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: device topology, session events, buffer size limits

The device topology was a stub: one connector of "Physical_Internal" whose
other methods were E_NOTIMPL, so no program could reach the endpoint's
jack, volume or mute controls (IKsJackDescription, IAudioVolumeLevel,
IAudioMute) the way the documentation of device topologies shows.
IAudioSessionControl took IAudioSessionEvents and never told them;
IAudioSessionManager2's session and duck notifications were E_NOTIMPL;
IAudioClient2::GetBufferSizeLimits was E_NOTIMPL.

- The endpoint's topology has one connector, linked to its adapter's
  bridge connector (the jack); the adapter's topology has a stream
  connector, a volume and a mute subunit and the jack, in signal order
  (render: stream, volume, mute, jack; capture the other way).
  IDeviceTopology (connectors, subunits, GetPartById, GetDeviceId,
  GetSignalPath), IConnector (type from the form factor, data flow,
  connections and the IDs connected to; software links of the stream
  connector), IPart (names, local and global IDs, part and node types,
  control interfaces, parts incoming and outgoing, the topology),
  ISubunit, IControlInterface, IPartsList.
- IAudioVolumeLevel (dB per channel) and IAudioMute are the endpoint's
  volume; their change callbacks (IControlChangeNotify) are told when it
  changes, with the event context. The jack describes itself
  (IKsJackDescription, IKsJackDescription2) from the endpoint's form
  factor and speakers.
- IAudioSessionEvents are told of display name, icon, grouping, simple
  and channel volume changes (with the event context) and of the
  session's state as its streams start, stop and go;
  IAudioSessionNotification of new sessions; duck notification sinks are
  kept (nothing ducks other sessions here).
- GetBufferSizeLimits: from the engine's period to two seconds, for a
  supported format. The class factory keeps its lock count.

Wine's mmdevapi tests: mmdevenum 72 tests, no failures; render and
capture as before.

Gate: test/audiotopo-gate.sh (test/audiotopo-probe.c; skips without an
audio endpoint). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_CONTROL_CALLBACKS
(mmdevapi/topology.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_SESSION_EVENTS (mmdevapi/session.c,
mmdevapi/audiosessionmanager.c).
