+/* Stained Glass OS 1666. An endpoint's device topology is what the
+ * documentation of device topologies describes for a simple adapter: the
+ * endpoint's own topology holds one connector, linked to the bridge
+ * connector (the jack) of its adapter's topology; that topology carries
+ * the signal between a stream connector and the jack through a volume and
+ * a mute subunit:
+ *
+ *   render:  stream connector -> Volume -> Mute -> jack  ==  endpoint
+ *   capture: jack -> Volume -> Mute -> stream connector; endpoint == jack
+ *
+ * The volume and mute controls (IAudioVolumeLevel, IAudioMute) are the
+ * endpoint's volume (IAudioEndpointVolume), and their change callbacks are
+ * told when it changes; the jack describes itself (IKsJackDescription,
+ * IKsJackDescription2) from the endpoint's form factor and speakers. */
+
+#define COBJMACROS
+
